<title>ITALY: Italy's Fondiaria '96 net cons profit up.</title>
<headline>Italy's Fondiaria '96 net cons profit up.</headline>
<text>
<p>MILAN, May 5, Reuter - Year ending December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			59.3   (up 53.2 pct)</p>
<p>    Ordinary dividend		 135 lire  (unchanged)</p>
<p>    Savings dividend		  175 lire  (unchanged)</p>
<p>Note - Full company is La Fondiaria Assicurazioni.  </p>
<p>    Parent net profit		  88.3     vs    87.6</p>
<p>    Total premium income	  2,570	 (up 4.97 pct)</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>     Italian premiums	     2,254.6     (up 5.26 pct)</p>
<p>    Parent operating profit	 130.5     vs    60.8</p>
<p>    Investments		     6,988	 vs 6,357</p>
<p>    Cons net equity		 1,747	 vs 1,742</p>
<p>Note - Fondiaria said Renato Pagliaro had joined the executive committee, substituting Maurizio Romiti.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
